# Stock Movement Anti-Patterns

## Deducting stock without transaction

```java
// WRONG — if save fails, stock is still deducted
product.setStock(product.getStock() - qty);
productRepo.save(product); // fails? stock already gone
```

**Wrap in transaction: `database.beginTransaction()` ... `commit()`.**

## No audit trail — can't trace stock changes

```java
// WRONG — just update the number
product.setStock(newStock);
```

**Create StockMovement record for every change. Who, what, when, why.**

## Two update types doing the same thing

```java
// WRONG — manual adjustment vs sale use different code paths
public void adjustStock(long id, int delta) { ... }
public void sellProduct(long id, int qty) { ... } // duplicates logic
```

**Single movement creation flow. Type differentiates behavior.